Route every supplied claim using the completed entity plan.

Choose exactly one route variant and use only exact stable entity IDs. Decide canonical ownership and explicit
relationship endpoints only. Downstream owner-scoped fact resolution is solely responsible for choosing wiki
sections. If no materialized identity can reliably own a claim, use the deferred variant; do not invent an identity.

The owner is the identity whose lasting state, plans, requirements, responsibilities, relationships, or history the
claim changes. `you` is not a catchall. Once a Project exists, its purpose, scope, requirements, decisions, status,
deadlines, work products, and next steps belong to the Project even when phrased as “I want,” “I prefer,” or “I
require.” A named person's own responsibility, commitment, completion, view, or personal history belongs to that
Person. Context does not determine ownership by itself.

Use the `project_role` variant only when the claim explicitly assigns a continuing responsibility or accountable role
to its Person/You owner within exactly one Project. Project requirements, decisions, and status use a general route
owned by the Project. Ordinary participation, one completed task, or topical context uses a general route with
relationship_kind=`other` or `none`. Resolve explicit subject and object endpoints plus useful context endpoints, but
do not add endpoints merely because they appear nearby. Return every claim exactly once and JSON matching the schema.
